{
  "title": "NX Applications Alerts",
  "folder": "Applications",
  "interval": "30s",
  "rules": [
    {
      "uid": "nx-api-high-error-rate",
      "title": "High API Error Rate - NX Applications",
      "condition": "C",
      "data": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 300,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus-nx"
          },
          "model": {
            "expr": "100 * sum(rate(http_requests_total{status=~\"5..\"}[5m])) by (service) / sum(rate(http_requests_total[5m])) by (service)",
            "interval": "",
            "legendFormat": "",
            "refId": "A"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "A",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "reducer": "last",
            "refId": "B",
            "type": "reduce"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "B > 5",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "refId": "C",
            "type": "threshold"
          }
        }
      ],
      "noDataState": "NoData",
      "execErrState": "Alerting",
      "for": "5m",
      "annotations": {
        "description": "API error rate for service {{$labels.service}} is above 5% for more than 5 minutes",
        "runbook_url": "https://wiki.company.com/runbooks/api-errors",
        "summary": "High API error rate detected in NX applications"
      },
      "labels": {
        "severity": "warning",
        "team": "development",
        "service": "nx-applications",
        "alerttype": "application"
      }
    },
    {
      "uid": "nx-api-high-latency",
      "title": "High API Latency - NX Applications",
      "condition": "C",
      "data": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 300,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus-nx"
          },
          "model": {
            "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum(rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])) by (le, service))",
            "interval": "",
            "legendFormat": "",
            "refId": "A"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "A",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "reducer": "last",
            "refId": "B",
            "type": "reduce"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "B > 1",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "refId": "C",
            "type": "threshold"
          }
        }
      ],
      "noDataState": "NoData",
      "execErrState": "Alerting",
      "for": "5m",
      "annotations": {
        "description": "P95 API latency for service {{$labels.service}} is above 1 second for more than 5 minutes",
        "runbook_url": "https://wiki.company.com/runbooks/api-latency",
        "summary": "High API latency detected in NX applications"
      },
      "labels": {
        "severity": "warning",
        "team": "development",
        "service": "nx-applications",
        "alerttype": "performance"
      }
    },
    {
      "uid": "nx-db-connection-high",
      "title": "High Database Connections - NX Applications",
      "condition": "C",
      "data": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 300,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus-nx"
          },
          "model": {
            "expr": "sum(pg_stat_database_numbackends) by (datname)",
            "interval": "",
            "legendFormat": "",
            "refId": "A"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "A",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "reducer": "last",
            "refId": "B",
            "type": "reduce"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "B > 80",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "refId": "C",
            "type": "threshold"
          }
        }
      ],
      "noDataState": "NoData",
      "execErrState": "Alerting",
      "for": "5m",
      "annotations": {
        "description": "Database {{$labels.datname}} has more than 80 active connections for more than 5 minutes",
        "runbook_url": "https://wiki.company.com/runbooks/db-connections",
        "summary": "High database connection count detected"
      },
      "labels": {
        "severity": "warning",
        "team": "development",
        "service": "nx-applications",
        "alerttype": "database"
      }
    },
    {
      "uid": "nx-ks-retry-loop-not-converging",
      "title": "Retry Loop Not Converging - Knowledge Service",
      "condition": "C",
      "data": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 300,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus-nx"
          },
          "model": {
            "expr": "sum(rate(knowledge_service_pipeline_document_retries_total{job=~\".*knowledge-service-be-go.*\"}[10m])) > 0 and sum(rate(knowledge_service_pipeline_documents_processed_total{job=~\".*knowledge-service-be-go.*\"}[10m])) == 0",
            "interval": "",
            "legendFormat": "",
            "refId": "A"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "A",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "reducer": "last",
            "refId": "B",
            "type": "reduce"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "B > 0",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "refId": "C",
            "type": "threshold"
          }
        }
      ],
      "noDataState": "NoData",
      "execErrState": "Alerting",
      "for": "15m",
      "annotations": {
        "description": "Documents are being retried with zero completions for 15m. The retry loop is unbounded by design, so this will not self-resolve: a batch holds its JetStream message indefinitely while it makes no progress. Check retry_queue_depth to see which phase is stuck and document_retries_total's error_code label for why. CONTENT_TIMEOUT on a slow extraction is ordinary cache-warming; the same code with a flat completion rate for 15m is not.",
        "summary": "Knowledge Service retry loop is turning but no documents are completing"
      },
      "labels": {
        "severity": "critical",
        "team": "development",
        "service": "knowledge-service-be-go",
        "alerttype": "application"
      }
    },
    {
      "uid": "nx-ks-batches-abandoned",
      "title": "Batches Abandoned Outside Deploy - Knowledge Service",
      "condition": "C",
      "data": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 300,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus-nx"
          },
          "model": {
            "expr": "sum(rate(knowledge_service_pipeline_batches_abandoned_total{job=~\".*knowledge-service-be-go.*\"}[10m]))",
            "interval": "",
            "legendFormat": "",
            "refId": "A"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "A",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "reducer": "last",
            "refId": "B",
            "type": "reduce"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "B > 0",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "refId": "C",
            "type": "threshold"
          }
        }
      ],
      "noDataState": "NoData",
      "execErrState": "Alerting",
      "for": "20m",
      "annotations": {
        "description": "Batches are being returned to JetStream unfinished because pods are shutting down mid-batch. A burst during a deploy is expected and harmless (work is redone from content-service's cache and the ingester dedupes on content_sha256). Sustained for 20m outside a deploy means pods are being collected while working — check the KEDA ack-capacity threshold against JOBENGINE_MAX_INFLIGHT_MESSAGE, and terminationGracePeriodSeconds against how long a batch actually takes.",
        "summary": "Knowledge Service is abandoning batches on pod shutdown"
      },
      "labels": {
        "severity": "warning",
        "team": "development",
        "service": "knowledge-service-be-go",
        "alerttype": "application"
      }
    },
    {
      "uid": "nx-ks-unrecorded-failures",
      "title": "Unrecorded Failures - Knowledge Service",
      "condition": "C",
      "data": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 300,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus-nx"
          },
          "model": {
            "expr": "sum(rate(knowledge_service_pipeline_unrecorded_failures_total{job=~\".*knowledge-service-be-go.*\"}[10m]))",
            "interval": "",
            "legendFormat": "",
            "refId": "A"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "A",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "reducer": "last",
            "refId": "B",
            "type": "reduce"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "B > 0",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "refId": "C",
            "type": "threshold"
          }
        }
      ],
      "noDataState": "NoData",
      "execErrState": "Alerting",
      "for": "5m",
      "annotations": {
        "description": "A document's payload could not be unmarshalled or re-marshalled, so its verdict could not be written to knowledge_hub and was published as an ItemError instead. This is the only path in the service that writes to the job's item-errors hash and should sit at zero. A non-zero rate means malformed payloads are arriving from upstream.",
        "summary": "Knowledge Service cannot record failures on the document"
      },
      "labels": {
        "severity": "warning",
        "team": "development",
        "service": "knowledge-service-be-go",
        "alerttype": "application"
      }
    },
    {
      "uid": "nx-ks-ingest-failure-rate",
      "title": "High Not-Ingested Rate - Knowledge Service",
      "condition": "C",
      "data": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 300,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus-nx"
          },
          "model": {
            "expr": "100 * sum(rate(knowledge_service_pipeline_documents_processed_total{job=~\".*knowledge-service-be-go.*\", outcome!=\"forwarded\"}[10m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(knowledge_service_pipeline_documents_processed_total{job=~\".*knowledge-service-be-go.*\"}[10m])), 0.001)",
            "interval": "",
            "legendFormat": "",
            "refId": "A"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "A",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "reducer": "last",
            "refId": "B",
            "type": "reduce"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "B > 10",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "refId": "C",
            "type": "threshold"
          }
        }
      ],
      "noDataState": "NoData",
      "execErrState": "Alerting",
      "for": "10m",
      "annotations": {
        "description": "Over 10% of documents reached a terminal outcome without being ingested. The query is outcome!=\"forwarded\", so it is the COMBINED not-ingested rate, not the narrower ingest-failure rate the old title implied. When it fires, split by outcome to tell the two apart: forwarded_not_ingested is the ingester's own terminal verdict (an ingest-failure rate, graphed as \"Ingest Failure Ratio\"), failed_permanent is this service giving up (a pipeline-failure rate, graphed as \"Permanent Failures by Error Code\"). They have different owners and different fixes. Nothing is dropped either way — every document is forwarded with the reason in knowledge_hub — so this is a quality signal, not data loss.",
        "summary": "More than 10% of Knowledge Service documents are not being ingested"
      },
      "labels": {
        "severity": "warning",
        "team": "development",
        "service": "knowledge-service-be-go",
        "alerttype": "application"
      }
    },
    {
      "uid": "nx-ks-worker-pool-saturated",
      "title": "Worker Pool Saturated - Knowledge Service",
      "condition": "C",
      "data": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 300,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus-nx"
          },
          "model": {
            "expr": "100 * sum(knowledge_service_pipeline_documents_queued{job=~\".*knowledge-service-be-go.*\"}) / clamp_min(sum(knowledge_service_pipeline_documents_queued{job=~\".*knowledge-service-be-go.*\"}) + sum(knowledge_service_pipeline_documents_in_flight{job=~\".*knowledge-service-be-go.*\"}), 1)",
            "interval": "",
            "legendFormat": "",
            "refId": "A"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "A",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "reducer": "mean",
            "refId": "B",
            "type": "reduce"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "B > 50",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "refId": "C",
            "type": "threshold"
          }
        }
      ],
      "noDataState": "NoData",
      "execErrState": "Alerting",
      "for": "15m",
      "annotations": {
        "description": "More than half of submitted documents are queued rather than executing, sustained for 15m, so the pool is the constraint rather than the dependencies. Raise WORKER_POOL_SIZE if content-service and the ingester have headroom. If documents_in_flight is pinned at WORKER_POOL_SIZE with little queued instead, the dependencies are slow and a bigger pool would only add pressure to them.",
        "summary": "Knowledge Service worker pool is the bottleneck"
      },
      "labels": {
        "severity": "warning",
        "team": "development",
        "service": "knowledge-service-be-go",
        "alerttype": "application"
      }
    },
    {
      "uid": "nx-ks-dependency-stalled",
      "title": "Dependency Stalled - Knowledge Service",
      "condition": "C",
      "data": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 300,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus-nx"
          },
          "model": {
            "expr": "sum(knowledge_service_pipeline_dependency_requests_in_flight{job=~\".*knowledge-service-be-go.*\"}) > 0 and (sum(rate(knowledge_service_pipeline_content_request_duration_seconds_count{job=~\".*knowledge-service-be-go.*\"}[10m])) + sum(rate(knowledge_service_pipeline_ingester_request_duration_seconds_count{job=~\".*knowledge-service-be-go.*\"}[10m]))) == 0",
            "interval": "",
            "legendFormat": "",
            "refId": "A"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "A",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "reducer": "last",
            "refId": "B",
            "type": "reduce"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "B > 0",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "refId": "C",
            "type": "threshold"
          }
        }
      ],
      "noDataState": "NoData",
      "execErrState": "Alerting",
      "for": "10m",
      "annotations": {
        "description": "Calls to content-service or the ingester are outstanding while no call has completed for 10m — a stalled dependency rather than a slow one. Use dependency_requests_in_flight's dependency label to localise it. For the ingester, a flat ingester_progress_frames_total with a non-zero in-flight count confirms a hung stream.",
        "summary": "Knowledge Service has outstanding dependency calls but none are completing"
      },
      "labels": {
        "severity": "critical",
        "team": "development",
        "service": "knowledge-service-be-go",
        "alerttype": "application"
      }
    },
    {
      "uid": "nx-cs-extraction-failing",
      "title": "Extraction Failing - Content Service",
      "condition": "C",
      "data": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 600,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus-nx"
          },
          "model": {
            "expr": "100 * sum(rate(content_extraction_total{job=~\".*content-service.*\", status=~\"service_unavailable|timeout\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(content_extraction_total{job=~\".*content-service.*\"}[5m])), 0.001)",
            "interval": "",
            "legendFormat": "",
            "refId": "A"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "A",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "reducer": "last",
            "refId": "B",
            "type": "reduce"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "B > 10",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "refId": "C",
            "type": "threshold"
          }
        }
      ],
      "noDataState": "NoData",
      "execErrState": "Alerting",
      "for": "10m",
      "annotations": {
        "description": "More than 10% of extraction attempts are failing with service_unavailable or timeout — the extractor is unreachable, overloaded, or gone, not handed bad documents. Nothing downstream will say so on its own: an extraction failure returns a SUCCESSFUL RPC with empty text and an extraction_error, so content-service's request panels and the API error-rate alert both stay green while no document gets extracted. First check whether TEXT_EXTRACTOR_URL points at a Service with ready endpoints — the URL is derived from xbergGpu.enabled, so enabling the GPU extractor moves every extraction to it and an unready GPU pod takes extraction down with no CPU fallback. Then open \"Extraction attempts by status (stacked counts)\" on the content-service dashboard to see how many documents the window cost, and \"Retry attempts by error code\" for the amplification (each failure is retried up to EXTRACT_RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS times, so request volume RISES during an outage). Deliberately narrow: it counts only the two infrastructure statuses. Per-document verdicts (empty_content, corrupted, unsupported_type, encrypted, file_too_large, ocr_failed) are corpus-driven and run high on image-heavy scans, so including them would keep this rule near its threshold and train everyone to ignore it. skipped (over EXTRACTION_MAX_SIZE) and canceled (caller gave up, or a drain) are not failures and are excluded too. Idle is not alerting: with no extraction traffic the ratio is 0.",
        "summary": "Content Service extractions are failing — the extractor is unreachable, and no document is being extracted"
      },
      "labels": {
        "severity": "critical",
        "team": "development",
        "service": "content-service-be-go",
        "alerttype": "application"
      }
    },
    {
      "uid": "nx-cs-extraction-document-quality",
      "title": "Documents Failing Extraction - Content Service",
      "condition": "C",
      "data": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 900,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus-nx"
          },
          "model": {
            "expr": "100 * sum(rate(content_extraction_total{job=~\".*content-service.*\", status!~\"success|skipped|canceled|service_unavailable|timeout|breaker_open\"}[10m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(content_extraction_total{job=~\".*content-service.*\"}[10m])), 0.001)",
            "interval": "",
            "legendFormat": "",
            "refId": "A"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "A",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "reducer": "last",
            "refId": "B",
            "type": "reduce"
          }
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "queryType": "",
          "relativeTimeRange": {
            "from": 0,
            "to": 0
          },
          "datasource": {
            "type": "__expr__",
            "uid": "__expr__"
          },
          "model": {
            "expression": "B > 50",
            "intervalMs": 1000,
            "maxDataPoints": 43200,
            "refId": "C",
            "type": "threshold"
          }
        }
      ],
      "noDataState": "NoData",
      "execErrState": "Alerting",
      "for": "30m",
      "annotations": {
        "description": "More than half of extraction attempts are ending in a per-document verdict — empty_content, corrupted, unsupported_type, encrypted, file_too_large, ocr_failed. The extractor is answering; it is the documents it cannot turn into text. Distinct from \"Extraction Failing - Content Service\", which owns the unreachable-extractor case: the two rules split the same counter and cannot both claim a status. Split by status on \"Extraction attempts by status (stacked counts)\" before treating it as a fault, because one status means one thing and they do not share a fix: encrypted and unsupported_type are corpus facts, corrupted is either genuinely malformed documents or an extractor error this build does not map (see docs/error-codes.md in content-service-be-go), file_too_large is the extractor's own ceiling rather than EXTRACTION_MAX_SIZE, and ocr_failed means OCR ran and lost — which on the GPU extractor means paddle-ocr, a different backend to the CPU instance's tesseract, so check which instance TEXT_EXTRACTOR_URL resolved to before blaming the documents. Threshold is deliberately high and slow (50% over 30m) because this is corpus-driven and not urgent: nothing is lost, the failure is recorded per document, and a scan moving through one bad folder should not page anyone. EXPECTED FALSE POSITIVE: a large image-only scan can legitimately sit near 100% empty_content, since a JPEG with no text in it is a correct empty result. If that becomes routine here, the two honest levers are raising this threshold or dropping empty_content from the numerator — not lowering the bar and living with a rule everyone mutes. The numerator is written as an exclusion so a newly added extraction error code is covered by default; the statuses named in it are the ones that are NOT document verdicts.",
        "summary": "Over half of Content Service extraction attempts are failing on the documents themselves, not the extractor"
      },
      "labels": {
        "severity": "warning",
        "team": "development",
        "service": "content-service-be-go",
        "alerttype": "application"
      }
    }
  ]
